note as INDEX_POLICY_cross_store_consistency
  INDEX AND ACCESS-PATTERN POLICY
  - Delivery is at least once; target writes are idempotent by event id, entity version and payload hash.
  - Checkpoints are advanced only after the target write is durable.
  - Reconciliation compares canonical and target hashes and creates explicit drift events.
  - Deletion is complete only after every target is verified absent or explicitly blocked by legal hold.
end note

